{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.c2_times_quantumTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.c2_times_quantumTwo","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuantumTwoIdentity.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The c₂·[2]_q recursion: if c₂ = -1, then c₂ · [2]_q = -[2]_q.\n(Trivial but records the structural claim.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.neg_quantumTwo_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.neg_quantumTwo_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuantumTwoIdentity.lean#L69-L71","doc":"At q = 1, -[2]_q evaluates to -2.\nThis is the classical limit, matching G(0,1) from CuspWindingLattice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.neg_quantumTwo_eq'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.neg_quantumTwo_eq'","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuantumTwoIdentity.lean#L63-L67","doc":"Reformulation using the named definitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.neg_quantumTwo_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.neg_quantumTwo_eq","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuantumTwoIdentity.lean#L55-L61","doc":"**KEY IDENTITY.** -(q + q⁻¹) = -2 - (q-1)²/q for any nonzero q.\nEquivalently: -[2]_q = -2 - q·ℏ_q², NOT -2 - ℏ_q² (see the module\ndocstring: `ℏ_q² = (q-1)²/q²`, a factor of `q` smaller). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.qHbarSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.qHbarSq","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuantumTwoIdentity.lean#L41-L53","doc":"`q · ℏ_q² = (q - 1)² / q`, the combination appearing in the `[2]_q`\nidentity below.\n\n**This is NOT `ℏ_q²`, and the declaration used to be called `hbarSq` and\ndocumented as such** (bean `qou-6bla`). `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`, so\n`ℏ_q² = (q - 1)²/q²` — a factor of `q` smaller:\n\n    (hbarQ q)^2  = 0.0098171865\n    (q - 1)^2/q  = 0.0108968667      1.1100x larger\n\nat `q₀ = 1.1099785827513808`. The theorem below is correct as stated and is\nunchanged; only the name and the docstring's identification were wrong. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.quantumTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QuantumTwoIdentity.quantumTwo","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QuantumTwoIdentity.lean#L38-L39","doc":"Symmetric quantum integer [2]_q = q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0}]}